course: dictionary
lesson: 6988
title: One word, two meanings: paperclip
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A paperclip is a small piece of bent wire that holds sheets of paper together. Many words have more than one meaning, and context tells you which one the writer means. «Sam clipped the worksheets together with a paperclip.» Here the words worksheets and clipped show that it is the bent wire.
explain: On a computer, paperclip means something different: a small clip symbol that tells you to attach a file, for example in an email. Ask yourself what the sentence is about. If it is about paper, it is the wire. If it is about sending a file, it is the symbol.
explain: Paperclips appear in science too. A paperclip is attracted to a magnet because it is made of steel. «A paperclip laid gently can float» on water, because of surface tension, the pull between water molecules at the surface. Always check your meaning by putting it back into the sentence and seeing if it still makes sense.
fact: A paperclip is a small piece of bent wire.
fact: Paperclips are used to hold sheets of paper together.
fact: On a computer, the paperclip symbol means "attach a file".
fact: A paperclip is attracted to a magnet because it is made of steel.
fact: «The smallest shrews weigh about as much as a paperclip or two», so a paperclip is very light.
exercise: «Sam clipped the worksheets together with a paperclip.» What is a paperclip in this sentence? | A pond insect that walks on water | A kind of pencil case | *A small piece of bent wire that holds paper together | A tiny computer file
exercise: On a computer, the paperclip symbol in an email means what? | Delete the message | Make the email go faster | *Attach a file | Print the email
exercise: «The smallest shrews weigh about as much as a paperclip or two.» What does this sentence tell you about a paperclip? | It is heavier than an elephant | It is made of plastic | *It is very light | It can move by itself
test: Why does a paperclip stick to a magnet? | Because it is warm | Because it is made of paper | Because it is painted | *Because it is made of steel
test: «A paperclip laid gently can float» on water. Which idea explains why it floats? | Long chain molecules | Magnets | Pond skaters | *Surface tension
exam: Which two meanings does paperclip have? | A magnet and a steel elephant | A pond insect and a tiny shrew | *A small bent wire for holding paper, and a computer symbol for attaching a file | A polymer and a plastic chain
